Body:
There's an issue in the Gemma 4 chat templates in handling the system message sent by OpenCode. The chat template expects the system message to be a string, not a list of text content parts. That's at least part of the confusion these models are running into with OpenCode. Here's a local diff that gets the system prompt rendering properly instead of as an inline JSON array:

```diff
--- chat_template.jinja 2026-04-16 18:46:34.506453697 -0400
+++ gemma_4_e4b_chat_template.jinja     2026-04-16 18:36:00.864299411 -0400
@@ -186,7 +186,15 @@
     {%- endif -%}

     {%- if messages[0]['role'] in ['system', 'developer'] -%}
-        {{- messages[0]['content'] | trim -}}
+        {%- if messages[0]['content'] is string -%}
+            {{- messages[0]['content'] | trim -}}
+        {%- elif messages[0]['content'] is sequence -%}
+            {%- for item in messages[0]['content'] -%}
+                {%- if item['type'] == 'text' -%}
+                    {{- item['text'] | trim -}}
+                {%- endif -%}
+            {%- endfor -%}
+        {%- endif -%}
         {%- set loop_messages = messages[1:] -%}
     {%- endif -%}
```

This may not fix all issues, but it's definitely part of the problem.
